# User Experience Guidelines

## Loading States & Feedback
- Provide clear feedback for all user actions
- Implement proper loading indicators with progress when possible
- Show processing states during AI image generation
- Use skeleton loaders for content that's loading

## Error Handling UX
- Handle edge cases gracefully with helpful messages
- Provide specific error messages (file too large, unsupported format, etc.)
- Include retry options when appropriate
- Show fallback UI when operations fail

## File Upload Experience
```tsx
// Drag & drop with clear feedback
<div className="border-2 border-dashed border-gray-300 rounded-lg p-6
                hover:border-gray-400 transition-colors">
  <p className="text-center text-gray-600">
    Drag & drop your image here, or click to select
  </p>
</div>
```

## Accessibility Requirements
- Ensure keyboard navigation support
- Add proper ARIA labels and descriptions
- Use semantic HTML elements
- Provide alternative text for images
- Maintain proper color contrast ratios

## Mobile Experience
- Ensure responsive design across all devices
- Optimize touch targets for mobile (min 44px)
- Handle mobile file uploads appropriately
- Test on various screen sizes

## Progressive Enhancement
- Show upload area immediately
- Enable prompt input after image upload
- Activate generate button when both are ready
- Display results with download options

## Performance Feedback
- Show image processing progress when possible
- Provide estimated completion times
- Allow cancellation of long operations
- Cache results when appropriate